  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "The text 'we destroy the world and kill a lot of people' is mapped onto the Nazi Party assembly.",
  "description": "The textual statement 'we destroy the world and kill a lot of people' is directly projected onto the visual entity of the formal assembly in Nazi Germany. The assembly, composed of individuals in uniform and formal attire seated in rows under swastika banners, is presented as the embodiment of the 'we' in the text. The visual material represents the collective entity (the Nazi Party leadership and members) that is being described by the text as having committed global destruction and mass killings. This is an analogical mapping where the group of people in the image is mapped as the subject performing the actions described in the text.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
